:"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"5b37b264-92ad-4280-a4c2-2ef32820672b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"725cf014-e8e6-4e21-907d-d54c6c265ee5","agentId":"a4595b0bc175c26cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QbKEi4fvjvCYmVJEihFwPt","type":"tool_result","content":"1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"02ffb4fd-8f14-4693-9979-6e0d3e24f497","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:07:52.605Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6c_opus_round2.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Scope: the 19 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6c.txt`, in `staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`."," Source: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (PDF idx = printed + 11)."," ","-**Page images I opened** (renders in `staging/_renders/r2_6c_p*.png`): PDF 288, 299, 300, 301, 371, 372, 378, 515, 536 (130 dpi full pages); Fig 6.25 (PDF 365) and Figs 6.30-6.31 (PDF 375) at 300 dpi; Fig 6.24 (PDF 365) at 200 dpi. Text layer only: PDF 28-29, 35, 38, 305, 363, 364, 367-370, 373-377, 379, 438, 514.","+**Page images I opened** (renders in `staging/_renders/r2_6c_p*.png`): PDF 288, 299, 300, 301, 371, 372, 378, 515, 536 (130 dpi full pages); PDF 363, 367, 368 (110 dpi, to confirm the fixer's quotes added to the two GO-edited entries); Fig 6.25 (PDF 365) and Figs 6.30-6.31 (PDF 375) at 300 dpi; Fig 6.24 (PDF 365) at 200 dpi. Text layer only: PDF 28-29, 35, 38, 305, 364, 369, 370, 373-377, 379, 438, 514."," "," ## Entry table"," "]},{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | heuristic--sequential-accumulation-needs-4-6-week-stages-extensive-before-explosive | GO | Fixes landed. Both Inferences are labelled (\"so the 4-6 weeks is a minimum\", \"Bondarchuk agrees\"). The PDF 300-301 stage-level rule is quoted exactly against the images. \"The list follows the research with novices and athletes of average qualification\" is a fair unquoted description: on PDF 300 that phrase introduces the three conclusions, and the \"principles ... emerge\" heading follows them. The Fig 5.13 \"Jumps\" label is confirmed on the image. | Checked against the PDF 372 image: 4-6 weeks, 2 weeks, \"transient accumulation\" (italic), the reverse sequence giving a negative effect, the energy-potential mechanism. PDF 300 and 301 images. Baseline lines 106 and 180. |"," | framework--three-viewpoints-on-organising-endurance-development | GO | Unchanged since round 1, and round 1 checked it against the PDF 373 image. | Not re-opened. |"," | claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality | GO | The fix landed and the logic is now consistent. Read literally, p. 370 (anaerobic before aerobic) fits both p. 372 lists (PDF 372 image: positive \"aerobic exercises are done after glycolytic-anaerobic training (in small volume)\"; negative \"glycolytic-anaerobic exercises follow large volumes of aerobic work\"). It conflicts only with p. 373's aerobic-first sequential model. The slip reading is labelled Inference. Fixer disagreement 2 is justified: PDF 373 lists four citations (Naumenko 1978; Vavilov 1977; Serafimova 1974; Morzhevikov 1980), and p. 370 gives two of them. | Checked against the PDF 370 text: 3-4 months, up to 10 months, one month, HR 120-170, 2-3 months, about 4 months, \"not definitive\". PDF 372 image, PDF 373 text. |","-| principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue | GO | The added missing-idea passage is accurate: \"The training potential of the means employed decreases as the special work capacity increases\" and \"it is inappropriate to use highly stimulating means prematurely, because the body is functionally unprepared for them ... disturbance of the natural course of adaptation\" (PDF 368-369, printed 357-358, text layer). Small wording point, not blocking: \"closes the preceding passage\" is loose, because the Fig 6.28 caption and a conjugate-sequence paragraph come between the warning and 6.9.4. All links resolve. | Checked against the PDF 369-370 text: the homeostasis sentence, the ligamentous-joint sentence, the four sports, the five qualification citations, the intensity sentence, \"only after preliminary preparation with extensive low intensity loading\". |","+| principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue | GO | The added missing-idea passage is accurate: \"The training potential of the means employed decreases as the special work capacity increases\" and \"it is inappropriate to use highly stimulating means prematurely, because the body is functionally unprepared for them ... disturbance of the natural course of adaptation\" (PDF 368 image, PDF 369 text layer). Small wording point, not blocking: \"closes the preceding passage\" is loose, because the Fig 6.28 caption and a conjugate-sequence paragraph come between the warning and 6.9.4. All links resolve. | Checked against the PDF 369-370 text: the homeostasis sentence, the ligamentous-joint sentence, the four sports, the five qualification citations, the intensity sentence, \"only after preliminary preparation with extensive low intensity loading\". |"," | framework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state | GO (spot-checked) | None. The \"page image not opened\" note for PDF 379 is still honest. I checked the PDF 379 text: \"not especially complex\" and \"much smaller\" match. | Checked against the PDF 378 image: the three levels (italic labels), \"one or more years\", \"up to 5-6 months\", \"proportion of intensive means\", \"largely random and at times unpredictable\", \"not determined by the adaptation of the first two levels\", \"controllable\". Baseline lines 64 and 255 not re-opened (round 1 checked them). |"," | claim--annual-speed-strength-dynamics-depend-on-qualification | GO | Unchanged since round 1. | PDF 377 text re-read: 3 to 4 times a year, Pollock 1973, twice a month, the medium-qualification cause, the monocycle and bi-cycle patterns. |"," | case-study--triple-jumper-plantarflexors-depressed-while-thigh-extensors-high | GO (spot-checked) | None. | Checked against the PDF 378 image: the italic sentence (italic confirmed), Verkhoshansky 1988, the plantarflexor and thigh-extensor sentences, \"feels perfectly fit\", the prescription wording. `untested` fits. |"]},{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":7,"newStart":29,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | case-study--nedobyvailov-light-heavy-and-combined-loads-in-jumpers | GO | **Fix verified on the 300 dpi crop.** At about 10.5 px per point: absolute strength GP1 7.0, GP2 18.2, GP3 16.8; speed GP1 17.9, GP2 11.1, GP3 13.5; power GP1 6.0, GP2 14.2, GP3 20.0 (the bar top sits on the 20 gridline). The entry's values (7, 18, 17; 18, 11, 14; 6, 14, 20), its Example and its When NOT pair (17 vs 18) all match. No old value remains. | Checked: 7 weeks, the three load groups, \"metabolic cost\", the caption, \"Group 1, graph 2\" (PDF 365 text and crop). |"," | framework--temporal-and-qualitative-forms-of-the-training-effect | GO | Unchanged since round 1, and round 1 checked it against the images. | Not re-opened. |"," | heuristic--routine-artificial-restoration-can-blunt-adaptation | GO | All three fixes landed: the \"signal\" gloss is labelled Inference; the 15% sentence now says the text does not specify the group, with the confound as Inference; and there is a blank line before Example (mechanical check). The fixer's extra Example change (\"without saying in which group\") is correct against PDF 368: \"At the same time, the volume of the training load was increased by an average of 15%\". | Checked against the PDF 368 text: 24.2/18.9 vs 7.7/4.9%, swimmers, Kuchnyev 1977, Platonov 1980, 2-4% and 12-20% (Potapchenko 1979), Yakovlev 1971, Siff & Yessis 1992, Yevgenyev et al 1975, \"strictly regulated\". Baseline lines 151 and 153. |","-| claim--middle-distance-runners-need-strength-and-jump-training-benchmarks | GO | The added missing ideas 2 and 3 are quoted accurately from the PDF 367 text (external similarity \"often overemphasized\", squats \"justified\", \"not only conform to, but exceed, competition conditions ... strength component\") and the PDF 363 text (\"cannot simply be used in a very general way\", the rower or cyclist example, \"The emergence of specificity ... is not supported\"). The 6.9.3 heading is on PDF 367. The 1.3 vs 1.4 note checks (PDF 35 heading \"1.3 A Philosophy of Physical Training\", PDF 38 heading \"1.4 Specificity in Training\") and is labelled Inference. Optional: \"Section 6.8.3 sets the same frame from the other side\" is the writer's framing; it could start with \"Inference:\". | Checked: the 800 m benchmarks, 10.6-10.7 s, 9 m and 33-34 m, Zhdanovich 1980, Verkhoshansky & Sirenko 1982, \"archaic viewpoint\" (PDF 367-368 text). Baseline lines 122 and 123. |","+| claim--middle-distance-runners-need-strength-and-jump-training-benchmarks | GO | The added missing ideas 2 and 3 are quoted accurately from the PDF 367 image (external similarity \"often overemphasized\", squats \"justified\", \"not only conform to, but exceed, competition conditions ... strength component\") and the PDF 363 image (\"cannot simply be used in a very general way\", the rower or cyclist example, \"The emergence of specificity ... is not supported\"). The 6.9.3 heading is on PDF 367. The 1.3 vs 1.4 note checks (PDF 35 heading \"1.3 A Philosophy of Physical Training\", PDF 38 heading \"1.4 Specificity in Training\") and is labelled Inference. Optional: \"Section 6.8.3 sets the same frame from the other side\" is the writer's framing; it could start with \"Inference:\". | Checked: the 800 m benchmarks, 10.6-10.7 s, 9 m and 33-34 m, Zhdanovich 1980, Verkhoshansky & Sirenko 1982, \"archaic viewpoint\" (PDF 367-368 text). Baseline lines 122 and 123. |"," "," **Tally: GO 17, FIX 2, NO-GO 0.**"," "]},{"oldStart":58,"oldLine