{"parentUuid":"e880d9f9-a6f2-4a31-979e-98e7af6fa5f9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a4595b0bc175c26cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffq34ewFHfSCWFsrfVs7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** Of the 19 entries, 17 are GO, 2 need a FIX and none is NO-GO. Both fixes are one-sentence text edits, so no figure needs to be re-read.\n\n**Fixes still needed:**\n1. **`principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum`:** the sentence \"which reconciles those two readings; the PDF p. 305 figure is a separate quantity\" is the writer's own reasoning but has no \"Inference:\" label. It came from the round-1 suggested wording. The fix is to add the label.\n2. **`heuristic--within-session-order-of-explosive-means-matters-less-than-volume-and-contrast`:**\n   - **PDF 288 is overstated.** The entry says resistance plus plyometrics \"works best\". The page says it works \"even more effectively than plyometrics alone\".\n   - **PDF 299 is reported only in part.** The same page explains the novice null result by the athletes' low fitness. It then says \"A well-trained athlete can expect the preceding strength work to have a positive effect\", and calls that untested. The contested paragraph should carry this. The split between novices and trained athletes should be labelled Inference. `contested` still stands.\n\n**What the round-1 fixes look like now:**\n- **Figures:** I read both myself. Fig 6.25 at 300 dpi gives 7/18/17, 18/11/14 and 6/14/20, which matches the corrected entry. On Fig 6.30 the shaded block runs from about month 1.6 to 4.5, and the curve values hold.\n- **Other fixes:** all of them landed, and the fix log's claims match the files.\n- **Fixer disagreements:** all four are backed by the page.\n- **Addendum voice:** only two files use Addendum material (PDF 514-590), and both attribute it to Verkhoshansky.\n- **Within-session paragraph:** PDF 300, 301 and 371 each say what the entry says, checked on the page images. Stage-level and session-level rules are kept apart. The barbell = strength / jumping = speed-strength link is labelled Inference.\n- **Format:** every file has six section headers, and exactly six em dashes, one per header. There are no wrapped links and no review-history wording. All 83 wikilinks resolve.\n\n**GO entries I spot-checked against the page images:**\n- `framework--positive-and-negative-sequences-of-endurance-loading` (PDF 372)\n- `case-study--barbell-and-depth-jump-sequences-in-high-jumpers` (Fig 6.24 values re-measured)\n- `case-study--sirenko-double-peak-strength-means-for-middle-distance-runners` (PDF 378)\n- `case-study--triple-jumper-plantarflexors-depressed-while-thigh-extensors-high` (PDF 378)\n- `framework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state` (PDF 378)\n\nI also checked the two GO entries the fixer edited, against the PDF 363, 367 and 368 images.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- Three small optional polish items are listed in the report.\n- Out of scope: the fix log flags `heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next`, in both staging and the vault. It says \"the Addendum says\" without naming Verkhoshansky, and it needs to go to whoever owns that batch.\n\nReport: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6c_opus_round2.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_read_input_tokens":217055,"output_tokens":1196,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":824},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":217055,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":824,"ephemeral_1h_i